1436	## Intent
1437	
1438	**Problem:** Configurações' "Sua evolução" chart (spec-8-1) never shows the AI narrative paragraph FR-39 requires alongside it, and has no distinct state for when only that narrative fails.
1439	
1440	**Approach:** Add a second, independent fetch (`GET /dashboard/narrative`) with its own `Resource<String>` cubit. Render the resulting text below the chart only in the >30-entries state — the only scenario with a narrative in the prototype — with a dedicated "unavailable, tap to retry" message when just that fetch fails; the chart itself never degrades.
1441	
1442	## Boundaries & Constraints
1443	
1444	**Always:**
1445	- Call `dashboard-narrative-get` with `queryParameters: {'period': 'all'}` — same fixed value as `dashboard-aggregate-get` (spec-8-1 precedent).
1446	- New `DashboardNarrativeCubit extends Cubit<Resource<String>>`, mirroring `DashboardCubit`'s exact shape: `registerLazySingleton`, constructor-subscribes to `PendingEntryWriteTracker.confirmedWrites` (recompute on every entry write, same as the aggregate), `load()` is generation-guarded.
1447	- `AccountSettingsScreen.initState` calls `narrativeCubit.load()` unconditionally, alongside the existing `dashboardCubit.load()` — two independent fetches fired in parallel, neither awaiting the other.
1448	- `DashboardChartSection` renders the narrative section *only* inside its existing `totalCount > 30` branch — confirmed by `prototype-extract.md` (lines 110-113) and the raw prototype's `cenarioDashboard` enum (`Zero registros`/`Uma entrada`/`Mais de 30`): the AI narrative exists only in the >30 scenario; the `0`/`1`-count branches keep their current hardcoded messages untouched, never fetching or showing narrative text.
1449	- Narrative states inside that branch: `ResourceData<String>` → the text, styled with a new `DesignTokens.dashboardNarrativeTextStyle` (Karla 400 · 13/20, read off `cerne-prototype.html`'s dashboard narrative markup — no existing token matches) + `colorTextSecondary`; `ResourceError<String>` → "Não foi possível gerar o balanço agora" in the same style, plus a tappable "tentar novamente" in `colorAccent` that re-calls `narrativeCubit.load()` (verbatim prototype copy/behavior — `cerne-prototype.html`'s `retryNarrative`); `Idle`/`Loading` → render nothing, so the chart never waits on the narrative.
1450	- `DashboardNarrativeDto` mirrors the full contract (`text`, `generatedAt`), same "decode everything, domain narrows" precedent as `DashboardAggregateDto`; `toDomain()` returns only `text` as a plain `String` (one field — no new entity).
1451	- `DashboardRepository`/`DashboardRemoteDataSource`/`DashboardRepositoryImpl` each gain one new method (`getNarrative`) — same files, same thin-pass-through/decode-to-`malformedResponse` shape as `getAggregate`, not a parallel class.
1452	- `AccountSettingsScreen` announces a narrative `ResourceError` via its existing `_announce`, same as the chart's own error announcement (accessibility precedent, spec-8-1 round 2).
1453	
1454	**Ask First:** None. **Never:** couple the two `Resource`s into one state object; show narrative text or its error for `0`/`1`-count states; call `dashboard-narrative-get` from anywhere but `DashboardNarrativeCubit.load()`.
1455	
1456	## I/O & Edge-Case Matrix
1457	
1458	| Scenario | Input / State | Expected Output / Behavior | Error Handling |
1459	|----------|--------------|---------------------------|----------------|
1460	| >30 entries, narrative resolves | aggregate `>30`, narrative `Right(text)` | Chart + narrative text below it | N/A |
1461	| >30 entries, narrative fails | aggregate `>30`, narrative `Left(Failure)` | Chart renders normally; "Não foi possível gerar o balanço agora" + "tentar novamente" | Tap re-calls `load()`, no crash |
1462	| 0 or 1 entries | aggregate count `0`/`1` | Narrative fetch result never rendered; existing hardcoded messages unchanged | N/A |
1463	| Narrative fetch pending | `Idle`/`Loading` | No narrative section shown | N/A |
